// Abstract for the milestone example. A short paragraph summarising the
// doctoral project, the work completed in the first half, and the plan
// for the second half.

This halftime report summarises the first half of a doctoral project on
uncertainty quantification for groundwater models. A Fourier neural
operator surrogate was trained on 5000 simulation runs and embedded in an
adaptive Markov chain Monte Carlo loop, cutting inference time on the
synthetic benchmark from hours to minutes at the cost of a small drop in
acceptance rate. The remaining work benchmarks the approach against
ensemble Kalman methods and transfers the methodology to two real-world
catchments before the journal article and dissertation writing phase.
